			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2168468">
									

<p>if you create a mind capable of all of the actions we ascribe to consciousness, that believes it is a conscious mind and can simultaneously question that belief, what is left?</p>
<p>how do we know that whatever lies beyond the microwormholes is human consciousness, and not something else? i mean, one possibility that comes to mind, humanity cut themselves off from god, or a god, or a facsimile thereof. interesting story, but the claire's assumption that humanity has become p-zombies feels groundless.</p>
<p>can a p-zombie seek to reverse its state? if so, what is the distinction between the p-zombie and its former/future conscious versions?</p>

